// metajs-rt.metajs -- MetaJS's own layer 2.
//
// Every other language has a `<lang>-rt.metajs`; this is MetaJS's. Without it the
// metajs compiler would link only lib/runtime.ll (the C floor), so a body that moves
// out of runtime.c into languages/lib/runtime.metajs would reach the other fifteen
// languages' `-exe` builds through their `<lang>-rt.ll` and disappear from MetaJS's.
//
// It is deliberately THIN: it imports lib/runtime.metajs and exports nothing of its
// own, because the metajs compiler emits the generic js_* externs and the C floor
// answers all of them. Once `metajs-rt.ll` is linked next to `runtime.ll`, a body in
// runtime.metajs is reachable from all sixteen native builds, and a floor `js_*`
// upcall declared in runtime.c resolves in every link.
//
// Compile with:
//     mec languages/metajs-to-llvm-ir.abnf languages/lib/metajs-rt.metajs -q -rt-lib
// which is what tests/gen-metajs-rt-ll.sh does; the result is the checked-in
// languages/lib/metajs-rt.ll that metajs-to-llvm-ir.abnf links next to lib/runtime.ll
// when it builds an -exe. An explicit `-rt` REPLACES both, which is what keeps
// tests/metajs-link-stubrt.c standing in for the whole runtime in the link tests.
//
// -rt-lib exports every TOP-LEVEL `function js_*` of this file AND OF EVERY FILE IT
// IMPORTS (metajs-to-llvm-ir.abnf, the -rt-lib block). So the exports of
// runtime.metajs are what this module offers. None of them is emitted by the metajs
// compiler and none collides with a runtime.c definition; they are the shared layer-2
// surface of the other languages, riding along because the import is the point.
//
// THE ONE RULE FOR ADDING TO THIS FILE: a body that belongs to more than one
// language goes in lib/runtime.metajs, not here. This file is for what is MetaJS's
// alone - and so far that is nothing.
//
// The frozen-subset rules of every MetaJS source apply
// (docs/abnf-dialect-gotchas.md): no ASI, so every `return` carries its value on the
// same line, and a value-less early return is braced.

// The shared layer-2 runtime, imported (not copied): the same text the other fifteen
// `<lang>-rt.metajs` files import.
import "./runtime.metajs"

// MetaJS's own exports go here. There are none yet; the import above supplies the
// export surface -rt-lib requires.
